  "invariant": "An acknowledged sign-out invalidates the selected or all persisted session credentials and their access tokens across WEB4-WEB10; unrelated avatar state is preserved; failed persistence never reports success.",
  "findings": [
    "Both Core logout methods return simulated success without persistence.",
    "Access JWT issuance in four authentication paths and refresh precedes the session save; JWTs lack persisted session/provider binding.",
    "WEB4 has a strict existing avatar read but no session-revocation validation.",
    "WEB5 and WEB7-WEB10 assign the authenticated principal before the avatar read and continue when the read returns an error or null.",
    "WEB6 validates cryptographic identity without an avatar/session lookup; do not claim the fix has no additional lookup across all services.",
    "Signed V2 refresh envelopes already bind the stored refresh credential to its acknowledged serving provider. New validation must use that authority, avoiding stale replica acceptance.",
    "Current stable public session IDs are SHA256(avatar GUID D + newline + stored refresh token); do not expose raw refresh tokens as access claims."
  ],
  "nextImplementation": [
    "Centralize the stable non-secret credential identity and session-bound JWT contract; mint the response JWT only after acknowledged session persistence.",
    "Validate exact session identity, active avatar and credential state at its authoritative provider across all seven APIs; publish identity to the request only after validation.",
    "Implement selected/global revocation with acknowledged provider-bound optimistic writes; concurrent sign-in/refresh or profile changes must not resurrect revoked sessions or be overwritten.",
    "Use a controlled issuer/validator rollout with an explicit legacy-token retirement boundary; do not permanently accept unbound tokens as a fallback. Account for configured token lifetimes rather than assuming 15 minutes.",
    "Enable the OPORTAL control only after real native HTTP checks prove access and refresh rejection, account isolation, persistence failure handling and unchanged unrelated state."
  ],
